    "terrainName": "berlin",
    "description": "What: Simulated devices SD-S5c (§3.13d D-119 with the designator as the receiver). The Observer carries a laser rangefinder (kit 1) and a laser target designator (kit 2), linked both ways. A scripted trainee possesses him, ranges a marker 450 m away through the rangefinder, presses its SEND chip, then binds his view to the designator and switches it on. Judge: (1) before SEND the designator holds no target; (2) after it the designator holds the marker's point (within 2 m), its range (~450 m) and the sender's type; (3) the designator's HUD shows the received-target cue - TARGET and 'from LASER RANGEFINDER (linked)'. Fail: the point lost or wrong, or no cue. Check: scripts/scenario-regression.sh dv-ltd-linked"
  },
